; ACCEPTANCE TEST for the generated `stmt` primitives.
;
; `SetLastError` returns VOID and takes one argument, which is 3.5% of the flat
; Win32 API that the survey refused and the target format could always say: a
; statement's value IS its first argument. Round-tripped through `GetLastError`,
; which was already declarable, so the answer is checked rather than assumed.
(use windows/kernel32 as k)
(use win/errhandlingapi as e)
(use win/fmt as fmt)
(export main)
; The comparison rather than the value, because a host result is unbounded and
; ADR 0019 refuses arithmetic on it — which is the OTHER thing the surveys
; located, and not what this test is about.
(def main (fn ()
  (seq (e.SetLastError 4242)
       (fmt.print-int (if (= (k.GetLastError) 4242) 1 0)))))
